From: Aishwarya R <aishwarya.r@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 10:54:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] DSCP: hostapd control interface for configuring DSCP policies

Introduce a new hostapd control interface command DSCP_POLICY to allow
runtime configuration of DSCP policies for associated stations.

Add parsing logic for DSCP policy parameters including DSCP value,
classifier mask, IP version, IP addresses, ports, and domain name. Add
support for both IPv4 and IPv6 classifiers.

Add support to validate input parameters and construction of frame
classifiers.

An example dscp_policy command usage:

hostapd_cli -i <wlanX> dscp_policy <sta_addr> <policy_id=>
<request_type=> <dscp=> [classifier_mask=] [ip_version=] [src_ip=]
[dst_ip=] [src_port=] [dst_port=] [protocol=] [domain_name=] [reset=]

Supported parameters:
- policy_id=<0-255>: Unique identifier for the DSCP policy
- request_type=<add/update/remove>: Indicates whether to add, update
                                    or remove the policy
- dscp=<0-63>: DSCP value
- classifier_mask=<bitmask>: Specifies TCLAS fields to match
- ip_version=<4/6>: IP version for classifier
- src_ip=<IPv4/IPv6 address>: Source IP address
- dst_ip=<IPv4/IPv6 address>: Destination IP address
- src_port=<0-65535>: Source port
- dst_port=<0-65535>: Destination port (mutually exclusive with dst_port)
- start_port=<0-65535>: Start of port range
- end_port=<0-65535>: End of port range
- protocol=<0-255>: Transport protocol
- domain_name=<string>: domain name (max 255 characters)
- reset=<0|1>: Flag to reset DSCP policy for the station

Backport of hostap commit cd5c149a6f87. OpenWrt context: ctrl_iface.c,
hostapd_cli.c: placed after the AFC commands of the 2.12 branch;
sta_info.h: placed after the bss_color_in_use field of OpenWrt's patch
174.

Signed-off-by: Aishwarya R <aishwarya.r@oss.qualcomm.com>
